WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.000
There’s a new Game of Thrones spinoff show&nbsp;
in development about Aegon’s Conquest – the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.480
story of how the Targaryens first took over&nbsp;
Westeros. There have been previous attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.680
to make an Aegon’s Conquest show, but now&nbsp;
it’s in development with a new writer.&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.240
So there are now at least six Game of Thrones&nbsp;
spinoff shows in development. House of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.200
Dragon Season 2 will air this year. A Knight of&nbsp;
the Seven Kingdoms has been greenlit – about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.160
adventures of Dunk and Egg. There’s an&nbsp;
animated show in development about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.440
voyages of the Sea Snake. And there are two&nbsp;
more animated projects in development – one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.560
of these might be The Golden Empire, about&nbsp;
Yi Ti, the Game of Thrones version of China.&nbsp;

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.440
There was a sequel show about&nbsp;
Jon Snow in development,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.920
led by Kit Harington. But it’s not clear if&nbsp;
that show is still being made. There was also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:49.200
a show about Nymeria in development – about&nbsp;
an ancient eastern princess. Finally there’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.800
a stage show about the tourney of Harrenhal&nbsp;
being made which might open late this year.&nbsp;

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:58.440
We’ve made videos about most of these&nbsp;
stories on our YouTube channel Alt Shift X.

